title: The General Election
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: time >= next_election_time
on-arrival: {!
// polling error on election night: up to 1.5 points either way on the Con-Lab gap
Q.apply_poll_error = 1;
Q.poll_error = (Math.random() - 0.5) * 3;
Q.final_poll_con = Q.con_votes;
Q.final_poll_lab = Q.lab_votes;
Q.final_poll_lib = Q.lib_votes;
Q.was_in_government = Q.con_in_government;
if (Q.time >= 61) {
    Q.new_boundaries = 1;
}
if (Q.new_boundaries) {
    Q.total_seats = 650;
    Q.majority_line = 326;
    Q.unionist_seats = 15;
}
!}
on-departure: month_actions += 1
set-jump: results
face-image: img/events/polling_station.jpg

# Low priority: this event only appears after every other event this month is resolved.

= Polling Day, [+ month : month +] [+ year +]

The polls have closed. The final opinion polls had us on [+ final_poll_con +]%, Labour on [+ final_poll_lab +]% and the [+ lib_name +]s on [+ final_poll_lib +]%. [? if autumn_election_1978 and n_elections = 0 : Callaghan's gamble on an autumn election is about to be judged. ?][? if no_confidence_won and n_elections = 0 : The election our motion forced is about to be decided. ?][? if was_in_government : After [+ months_in_office +] months in Downing Street, the country gives its verdict on your government. ?]

Party workers gather around the television at Central Office as the first results come in.

- @election_algorithm: Watch the results come in.

@results
on-arrival: {!
Q.apply_poll_error = 0;
Q.poll_error = 0;
Q.general_election_held = 1;
Q.n_elections += 1;
Q.last_election_time = Q.time;
// the new House of Commons
Q.con_mps = Q.con_seats;
Q.lab_mps = Q.lab_seats;
Q.lib_mps = Q.lib_seats;
Q.snp_mps = Q.snp_seats;
Q.pc_mps = Q.pc_seats;
Q.ni_mps = Q.ni_seats;
Q.other_mps = Q.other_seats; // the Speaker is counted in their old party's seat
Q.con_majority = 2 * Q.con_mps - Q.total_seats;
Q.con_short = Q.majority_line - Q.con_mps;
Q.largest_party = (Q.con_mps >= Q.lab_mps) ? 'con' : 'lab';
Q.con_plus_lib = Q.con_mps + Q.lib_mps;
Q.con_plus_ni = Q.con_mps + Q.unionist_seats;
Q.final_election_reached = (Q.n_elections >= Q.final_election) ? 1 : 0;
Q.election_records.push({'date': new Date(Q.year, Q.month - 1),
                         'con': Q.con_mps, 'lab': Q.lab_mps, 'lib': Q.lib_mps,
                         'snp': Q.snp_mps, 'pc': Q.pc_mps, 'ni': Q.ni_mps});
// reset the campaign for next time
Q.election_called = 0;
Q.campaign_started = 0;
Q.manifesto_launched = 0;
Q.tv_debate_decided = 0;
Q.sun_endorsed = 0;
Q.in_campaign = 0;
// the next Parliament must be dissolved within five years
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 60;
Q.election_deadline_time = Q.time + 60;
Q.months_to_election = 60;
Q.next_election_month = ((Q.next_election_time - 1) % 12) + 1;
Q.next_election_year = 1978 + Math.floor((Q.next_election_time - 1) / 12);
!}
on-display: {!
var data = [
    {"id": "lab", "legend": "Labour", "name": "Labour", "seats": Q.lab_mps},
    {"id": "snp", "legend": "SNP", "name": "SNP", "seats": Q.snp_mps},
    {"id": "pc", "legend": "Plaid Cymru", "name": "Plaid Cymru", "seats": Q.pc_mps},
    {"id": "lib", "legend": Q.lib_name, "name": Q.lib_name, "seats": Q.lib_mps},
    {"id": "other", "legend": "Other", "name": "Other", "seats": Q.other_mps},
    {"id": "ni", "legend": "Northern Ireland", "name": "Northern Ireland", "seats": Q.ni_mps},
    {"id": "con", "legend": "Conservative", "name": "Conservative", "seats": Q.con_mps}
];
if (typeof window !== 'undefined' && typeof d3 !== 'undefined' && d3.parliament) {
    var width = 500;
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50;
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("commons").style.height = screenWidth / 2 + "px";
    }
    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#commons").datum(data).call(parliament);
}
!}
go-to: formation

= The New House of Commons

{!<svg id="commons" style="width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

{!<table>!}
{!<tr><td>Party</td><td>Vote</td><td>Seats</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#0087DC'> </div> !} **Conservative** {!</td><td>!} **[+ con_votes +]%** {!</td><td>!} **[+ con_mps +]** {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#DC241F'> </div> !} Labour {!</td><td>!} [+ lab_votes +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ lab_mps +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#FDBB30'> </div> !} [+ lib_name +] {!</td><td>!} [+ lib_votes +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ lib_mps +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#FDF38E'> </div> !} SNP {!</td><td>!} [+ snp_votes +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ snp_mps +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#008142'> </div> !} Plaid Cymru {!</td><td>!} [+ pc_votes +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ pc_mps +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#9999FF'> </div> !} Northern Ireland {!</td><td>!} {!</td><td>!} [+ ni_mps +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!</table>!}

[? if con_mps >= majority_line : **A Conservative majority of [+ con_majority +].** ?][? if lab_mps >= majority_line : **Labour has won a majority.** ?]

[? if con_mps < majority_line and lab_mps < majority_line and largest_party == "con" : **A hung parliament.** We are the largest party, [+ con_short +] seats short of a majority. ?][? if con_mps < majority_line and lab_mps < majority_line and largest_party == "lab" : **A hung parliament.** Labour is the largest party. ?]

@formation

- @majority
- @unionist_deal
- @liberal_deal
- @minority
- @concede

@majority
title: Form a Conservative government.
view-if: con_mps >= majority_line
on-arrival: result_type = 1; govt_type = 1
go-to: game_over if final_election_reached = 1; taking_office if final_election_reached = 0

@unionist_deal
title: Govern with the support of the Ulster Unionists.
subtitle: Conservatives + Unionists: [+ con_plus_ni +] seats.
unavailable-subtitle: Conservatives + Unionists: [+ con_plus_ni +] seats. Our relations with the Unionists are not good enough.
view-if: con_mps < majority_line and largest_party == "con" and con_plus_ni >= majority_line
choose-if: uup_relation >= 50
on-arrival: result_type = 2; govt_type = 2; partner_dissent = 0
go-to: game_over if final_election_reached = 1; taking_office if final_election_reached = 0
achievement: ulster_deal

@liberal_deal
title: Open talks with [? if alliance_formed : the Alliance ?][? if not alliance_formed : David Steel ?].
subtitle: Conservatives + [+ lib_name +]s: [+ con_plus_lib +] seats.
unavailable-subtitle: Conservatives + [+ lib_name +]s: [+ con_plus_lib +] seats. They won't deal with us.
view-if: con_mps < majority_line and largest_party == "con" and con_plus_lib >= majority_line
choose-if: lib_relation >= 50

The price of support, vote by vote, is a real move towards proportional representation.

- @liberal_deal_accept: Concede a Speaker's Conference on electoral reform.
- @formation: Refuse, and look for another way.

@liberal_deal_accept
on-arrival: result_type = 3; govt_type = 3; partner_dissent = 0; electoral_reform_promise = 1; right_dissent += 10; dry_dissent += 5
go-to: game_over if final_election_reached = 1; taking_office if final_election_reached = 0
achievement: lib_con

@minority
title: Form a minority government and dare the others to bring it down.
view-if: con_mps < majority_line and largest_party == "con"
on-arrival: result_type = 4; govt_type = 4; partner_dissent = 2
go-to: game_over if final_election_reached = 1; taking_office if final_election_reached = 0

@concede
title: Concede defeat.
view-if: largest_party == "lab"
on-arrival: result_type = 5; con_in_government = 0; govt_type = 0
go-to: game_over if final_election_reached = 1; back_to_opposition if final_election_reached = 0
